<title>UK: British Sugar denies Lonrho Sugar bid talk.</title>
<headline>British Sugar denies Lonrho Sugar bid talk.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Sugar Plc, the sugar arm of Associated British Foods on Thursday denied a newspaper report saying it was considering a possible bid for Lonrho Sugar Corp Ltd.</p>
<p>&quot;We're not doing anything in South Africa at all,&quot; one company spokesman said.</p>
<p>Lonrho Sugar said in a brief statement earlier on Thursday it was involved in talks which could affect its share price if successful, but gave no further details.</p>
<p>The report published in South Africa's Business Day newspaper said Tate and Lyle could also be considering a bid for Lonrho's South African sugar company.</p>
<p>Tate and Lyle declined comment.</p>
<p>--Simon Gardner, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
